# Sentry control plane environment.
#
# Copy to .env on the server and fill in. NEVER commit the real .env.
# Generate each secret with: openssl rand -base64 48
#
# Note: `docker compose config` interpolates and prints these values, so avoid
# running it where the output could be captured.

# --- PostgreSQL ---
POSTGRES_USER=sentry
POSTGRES_DB=sentry
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=

# --- Gateway ---
# Signs access, node, and work-order tokens. Must be at least 32 bytes; the
# Gateway refuses to start with a shorter one.
SENTRY_SIGNING_KEY=
# Password recovery uses a separate token file at
# data/gateway/sentry-recovery.token. Generate it once with
# ./provision-recovery-bridge.sh; never reuse SENTRY_SIGNING_KEY.
# IANA zone the cron scheduler evaluates job schedules in. The container clock
# is UTC, so without this a "0 8 * * *" morning brief fires at 08:00 UTC —
# hours off the operator's morning. Read once at Gateway startup.
SENTRY_CRON_TIMEZONE=America/New_York

# --- Hermes runtime ---
# Required by the Hermes API server even on a loopback bind.
HERMES_API_KEY=
# Pin the runtime. Production never tracks `latest`. Optional: the repo already
# defaults to this release (hermes/Dockerfile + compose.yaml); set it here only
# to run a different one.
HERMES_VERSION=0.19.0
# Must match the host owner of ./data so the bind mount is writable without root.
HERMES_UID=1000
HERMES_GID=1000

# The Sentry profile bound to this Hermes instance. Hermes selects its profile
# per process, so each additional profile needs its own container and port.
SENTRY_BOOTSTRAP_PROFILE_ID=
SENTRY_BOOTSTRAP_PROFILE_NAME=sentry-personal

# --- Public reach (Cloudflare Tunnel) ---
# The tunnel the cloudflared sidecar runs. Not a secret — the credentials file
# it pairs with is (deploy/linux/cloudflared/creds.json, 0600, gitignored).
# Created by ./create-tunnel.sh, which also writes the DNS record and the
# credentials file. Ingress lives in cloudflared/config.yml.
SENTRY_TUNNEL_ID=

# --- Inference provider ----------------------------------------------------
# Production uses the Nous Portal OAuth stored inside each Hermes profile:
#   docker compose exec hermes hermes auth add nous --type oauth
# No metered provider API key is required for the default route or managed
# image generation.
# Optional alternate providers:
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Claude SUBSCRIPTION (Pro/Max) rather than metered API billing. Mint with
#   claude setup-token
# on a machine already signed in to Claude, then paste the token here and
#   docker compose up -d hermes
#   ./attach-subscription.py anthropic --model <model-id>
# to publish it as a pickable model. See systemd/README.md.
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
